-- title:
--   j-invariant of cyclic quotients of a base-changed Tate curve
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and let $\Lambda$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,F$; let $q,\ell$ be primes and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, $\ell\nmid M'$ and $M'\neq 0$ in $F$, and let $\zeta\in F$ be a primitive $M'$-th root of unity. Let $C$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $\Lambda$ and let $W$ denote the base change to $\Lambda$ of [`ModularCurve.tateBase F (q * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L46), that is, of the image of the formal Tate curve `tateLaurent F` under the ring homomorphism `qExpand F (q * ℓ)` substituting $\mathfrak q\mapsto \mathfrak q^{q\ell}$. Let $g$ be an affine point of $C\bullet W$ such that $n\cdot g=0$ if and only if $M'\mid n$, and such that for every $n$ with $M'\nmid n$ the point $n\cdot g$, transported back to $W$ by the coordinate change `vcFun C`, is the affine point whose coordinates are the images under $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,F\to\Lambda$ of the two components of `toricPoint F (q * ℓ) (ζ ^ n)`. Let $d$ be a nonzero divisor of $M'$. Then the quantity $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the curve `cyclicQuotientCurve` attached to $C\bullet W$, the subgroup generated by $(M'/d)\cdot g$ and the parameter $d$ equals the image under $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,F\to\Lambda$ of `jqNModC F (q * ℓ * d)`, the $\mathfrak q$-expansion $\mathfrak q^{-1}+\dots$ of $j$ with $\mathfrak q$ replaced by $\mathfrak q^{q\ell d}$.
--
--   This is the computation of the $j$-invariant of the quotient of a Tate curve over $F((\mathfrak q^{q\ell}))$, presented in arbitrary Weierstrass coordinates over an extension field $\Lambda$, by the cyclic subgroup of order $d$ cut out inside the toric $M'$-torsion: the quotient is again a Tate curve, with parameter $\mathfrak q^{q\ell d}$. It feeds the identification of $j$-invariants at the cusps used for full-level structures, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.algebraMap_jqNModC_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_of_eq_map_tatePoint_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.algebraMap_jqNModC_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_of_eq_map_tatePoint_gamma0Pow).
-- source:
